From: tsh () mrc-lmb ! cam ! ac ! uk (Horsnell T ! )
Date: Tue, 31 Oct 2000 16:06:43 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: hwmgr
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97300943601942

Many thanks to Colin Walters, Tom Blinn and William Bochnik for
their replies. Colin pointed me to a Best Practice document at:

http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/faqs/publications/best_practices/BP_RECROOT/TITLE.HTM

which had the critical piece of information for me. What I needed to do after
booting the root image of my base machine to single-user, was to run
/sbin/mountroot. This updates the device database and allows subsequent
tidying with hwmgr and dsfmgr.

I find taking images much easier than the cloning methods described in the
Installation Guide -Advanced topics manual, especially if the
system you want multiple copies of is at all customised.

Phew! Thanks a lot guys.

Terry.

