Subject: SUMMARY: .Xdefaults for CDE
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97198191400751

Thanks to Bob Marcan, Arno Hahma and Colin Walters for their valued input.

> Prior to CDE I would add a line "xterm*pointerShape arrow"
> to the users .Xdefaults file.
> What file should be edited for CDE?

It can be as simple as adding the "correct" line to ~$USER/.Xdefaults...

For example "Dtterm*pointerShape: arrow" which I tried before posting however 
failed to use a capital "D". This works just fine.

Review /usr/dt/app-defaults/C/Dtterm, which is the system wide application 
default file for Dtterm. It explains more of the bits and pieces.

When customizing CDE you might have to set (and remember to reload with
xrdb) such resources in the dt (or .dt for local changes) directories
and files.  For example, to create a system-wide custom workspace manager
config file, you copy files from /usr/dt/config.... to /etc/dt/config
and customize them.

And of course don't forget this information is in the CDE Advanced User's Guide, 
available online at the URL below for your version of the OS.

http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/pub_page/doc_list.html

Thanks for all your help
/mark

