 First,

Timothy Brown: Confirmed that he has a few KGPSA-BC HBA's up and running on
ES40's running 5.0a. So that proved they should/could work.

 The majority of the responses indicated that I need to add "config_driver
emx" in the system config file.

 I had not done this as I assumed, that because the emx driver tried to
load, it was in there. The old "assume" pitfall again...

Dr. Tom Blinn sent me a email that contained a lot of information. Part of
which he stated that Tru64 would try to load the kernel driver "emx" even if
it was not in the system config file and that I should make sure that the
"config_driver emx" was in there. This confirmed what was happening on my
system.

 I then added the "config_driver emx", did a doconfig/reboot and the card is
working!

I received a few other comments on having problems with slot 1 and 2 on
PCI-0, so I moved the card out of these slots to be safe.

Thanks for everyone's help, we are up and running ;-) I may learn this Tru64
stuff yet..

