	Hi all,

	I got 3 responses :

Paul Henderson says : Check the permissions of the users' $HOME/.netscape
directories. I did it : all was ok

Stuart Whitby : Hi had this problem on Solaris

Sheila Hollenbaugh : 
This happened to us when we relocated some users home directories.  In the
$HOME/.netscape/preferences.js there were explicit paths to the old home
directories.  So you might want to check that the path to the bookmarks is
really in a directory that they are able to write in.


	So what I did : 

	- rename .netscape to old.netscape
	- run a new netscape from scratch which rebuild
	  .netscape and all its subdirectories
        - in netscapes bookmark, I made an import from
	  the old bookmark on the current bookmark is
	  now ok.

	Thanks for all whose helped

	JEAN

 

