>From: "Kristen Abbott" <abbott@zk3.dec.com>
>To: <chuacarlos@hotmail.com>
>Subject: RE: How to rename diskgroup name? (fwd)
>Date: Thu, 5 Oct 2000 15:28:59 -0400
>
>Hello;
>
>Your question was forwarded to me since I work on the LSM manual.
>
>There is no direct way to rename a disk group, but it can be done. You have
>to stop all activity on the volumes in the disk group, deport the disk
>group, and reimport it with a new name. Once the disk group is reimported,
>you can restart all its volumes. The entire process should not take long,
>but your volumes will be inaccessible for the duration.
>
>Note that this procedure does not cover any steps you might have to take
>before stopping the volumes; if they are used by AdvFS file domains or UFS,
>you need to unmount the file system and possibly remove the volumes from 
>the
>domain before deporting the disk group. It's up to you whether being able 
>to
>rename your disk group is worth this effort.
>
>The LSM-specific steps are:
>1. Stop the volumes in the disk group you want to rename.
>	# volume -g <diskgroup> stopall
>2. Deport the disk group.
>	# voldg deport <diskgroup>
>3. Reimport the disk group and give it a new name.
>	# voldg import -n newname <diskgroup>
>4. Restart the volumes.
>	# volume -g <new_diskgroup_name> startall
>
>Then you must reconfigure the AdvFS or UFS file systems (or the 
>appliations)
>to use the volumes as they were before.
>
>Hope this helps!
